<title>USA: US Xpress combines subsidiaries.</title>
<headline>US Xpress combines subsidiaries.</headline>
<dateline>CHATTANOOGA, Tenn 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Road hauler US Xpress said it has put two of its operating subsidiaries, Hall Systems and National Xpress Logistics, into its US Xpress operating subsidiary, part of a campaign to cut fixed costs by $12 million a year.</p>
<p>US Xpress, a trucking concern specializing in time-definite and expedited truckload services, serves many air freight shippers, the company said.</p>
<p>The logistics division is attempting to build a niche in the market fro deferred air freight services in the southeastern U.S.,it added. --Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax +44 171 542 5017</p>
